# ADIF & large artifacts
*.adi
# ...except ADIF's own published test logs. The rule above is there to keep a
# personal log from being added, and it is worth keeping for that. These two
# are the opposite kind of file: ADIF publishes them in the same resource zips
# as the spec exports this package already ships unmodified, every record in
# them is valid ADIF by definition, and they are what proves the validator does
# not reject a record ADIF itself issued.
#
# tests/data/ki7mt-sample.adi is tracked and stays tracked: it is a real
# extract, which is exactly what makes it useful as a known-good reference
# alongside ADIF's generated ones. It predates this rule, and .gitignore does
# not apply to a tracked file in any case.
!tests/data/ADIF_*_test_QSOs_*.adi
*.ndjson
*.jsonl
/tmp/
*.log

# local scratch
full.json
*.errors.json

